  "notes": "Same 4TU release as dataset_23: the 17 loose csv files repeat the ones zipped there. Test conditions (25/45 C, SOC window, charge and discharge C-rates) are in the file names; the cathode is described only as Ni-rich. aging_type corrected from \"calendar\" to \"cyclic\": every entity is a \"Cycl_...\" or \"DrivingAgeing...\" file (rate-based cycling or a drive-cycle profile), none is calendar aging - the old value was stale from when this dataset pointed at a different, superseded \"previous_record\" calendar-aging folder. dataset_23, the identical 4TU release repackaged, is already correctly \"cyclic\". Cell spec from LG's official INR18650 MJ1 3500mAh product specification. The author README claims cell-level temperature measurements, but every locally available measurement CSV header was checked and contains no temperature channel (17 loose CSVs in dataset_22, 18 archive CSVs in dataset_23). Local cell-temperature data are absent at this inspected source scope. The extracted cycle total is a count of current-sign discharge events because no cycle-index column is delivered; dynamic drive reversals may create many events within one aging cycle. It must not be used as a verified count of physical aging cycles."
 },
